2026-09-07 13:48:09 - car_buy_helper - INFO - Streaming response sent: {"message": {"type": "AI", "text": "I have consulted the **CarFinanceAgent** to calculate the loan breakdown for your \u20b912 lakh car purchase.\n\n### **Loan Summary**\n*   **Car Price:** \u20b912,00,000\n*   **Down Payment:** \u20b93,00,000\n*   **Loan Amount (Principal):** \u20b99,00,000\n*   **Interest Rate:** 9% per annum\n*   **Loan Tenure:** 5 Years (60 months)\n\n### **Financial Breakdown**\n*   **Monthly EMI:** **\u20b918,682**\n*   **Total Interest Payable:** **\u20b92,20,920**\n*   **Total Amount Paid (Principal + Interest):** **\u20b911,20,920**\n\n---\n\n### **Important Considerations & Assumptions:**\n1.  **On-Road Costs:** This calculation is based on the **loan amount** of \u20b99 lakh. Please remember that the \"Car Price\" of \u20b912 lakh usually refers to the Ex-Showroom price. You will need to account for Registration (RTO), Insurance, and TCS, which could add another \u20b91.5 to \u20b92 lakh to the total cost. Most banks only fund up to 90-100% of the *Ex-Showroom* price, not the *On-Road* price.\n2.  **Processing Fees:** Most banks charge a processing fee ranging from **\u20b92,500 to 1% of the loan amount**. This is usually deducted upfront from the loan disbursement.\n3.  **Pre-payment Charges:** Since you are looking at a 5-year tenure, check if the bank allows part-payments or foreclosure without heavy penalties. This can help you save significantly on the \u20b92.2 lakh interest if you have extra cash later.\n4.  **Credit Score:** The 9% interest rate is an estimate based on current market trends for used/new cars. If your credit score is below 750, the rate may be higher (10.5% - 13%), which would increase your EMI.\n\n**Would you like me to adjust the tenure to 3 or 7 years to see how it affects your monthly budget?**"}}
