2026-09-07 13:58:31 - car_buy_helper - INFO - Streaming response sent: {"message": {"type": "AI", "text": "To provide you with the best options, I have consulted the **CarSearchAgent** to identify vehicles that meet your specific criteria (Used, Diesel, Automatic, SUV, 2020+, <60k km, <15 Lakh).\n\nBased on the current market trends, here are the top recommendations that fit your requirements:\n\n### 1. Kia Sonet (Diesel AT)\n*   **Model Years:** 2020\u20132022\n*   **Approx. Price:** \u20b911.5 Lakh \u2013 \u20b914 Lakh\n*   **Why it fits:** It is one of the few compact SUVs in this price bracket that offers a proper **6-speed Torque Converter** automatic transmission with the diesel engine, rather than a jerky AMT.\n*   **Verdict: BUY**\n    *   *Reason:* Excellent engine-gearbox refinement, feature-rich interior, and good fuel efficiency. It is the most \"complete\" automatic experience in this budget.\n\n### 2. Tata Nexon (Diesel AMT)\n*   **Model Years:** 2020\u20132022\n*   **Approx. Price:** \u20b910.5 Lakh \u2013 \u20b913.5 Lakh\n*   **Why it fits:** Very popular in the used market with high availability. Offers a 5-star safety rating.\n*   **Verdict: CONSIDER**\n    *   *Reason:* While the car is robust and safe, the **AMT (Automated Manual Transmission)** is not as smooth as a traditional automatic. It is great for value, but test-drive it first to see if you are comfortable with the \"head-nod\" effect during gear shifts.\n\n### 3. Mahindra XUV300 (Diesel AMT)\n*   **Model Years:** 2020\u20132021\n*   **Approx. Price:** \u20b910 Lakh \u2013 \u20b912.5 Lakh\n*   **Why it fits:** Offers the most torque in its segment and a very spacious cabin (width-wise).\n*   **Verdict: CONSIDER**\n    *   *Reason:* Like the Nexon, it uses an AMT. It has excellent performance and safety, but the boot space is significantly smaller than rivals.\n\n### 4. Hyundai Creta / Kia Seltos (Diesel AT)\n*   **Model Years:** 2020 (Early models)\n*   **Approx. Price:** \u20b914.5 Lakh \u2013 \u20b916 Lakh (Might require negotiation to fit under 15L)\n*   **Why it fits:** These are a segment above the others. Finding a 2020+ Diesel AT under 60,000 km for strictly under 15L is challenging but possible with high-mileage examples or base automatic trims.\n*   **Verdict: NEGOTIATE**\n    *   *Reason:* If you find a well-maintained unit at 15L, it offers much better space and prestige. However, ensure the service history is verified as these are often driven heavily.\n\n---\n\n### Important Considerations\nTo give you a more precise evaluation and ownership cost breakdown, could you please provide:\n1.  **Your Location:** (Prices and availability vary significantly between cities like Delhi, Mumbai, or Bangalore).\n2.  **Intended Usage:** (How many km will you drive monthly? Diesel is best if you drive >1,500 km/month).\n3.  **Maintenance Expectations:** (Are you looking for low-cost service or are you okay with premium maintenance for better features?)\n\n### Next Steps\n*   If you have a specific listing in mind, I can call the **CarEvaluationAgent** to check if the price is fair.\n*   If you want to know about the long-term service costs of these models, I can call the **OwnershipCostAgent**.\n*   If you are ready to go for an inspection, I can call the **CarInspectionAgent** to provide a checklist for used diesel automatics."}}
